From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Stephan WEGENER <steph.wegener@gmail.com>
Date: Sat, 3 Oct 2026 11:10:29 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 18/25] [Onyx] A compositor on the V3D, stage 1: the page's
 layers as tiles, composited by gpucomp

USE(GRAPHICS_LAYER_ONYX): GraphicsLayerOnyx is a real GraphicsLayer (its properties, a grid of
512-pixel tiles kept over a window around what is seen, painted by Skia on the CPU), and
LayerTreeHostOnyx, in the web process, flushes the tree, paints the tiles that are new or dirty,
gives them to Onyx's gpucomp as textures and composites the layers (translations, rectangular
clips, opacity) straight into a kernel surface the UI process made and maps; a frame is told to
the UI process (DrawingAreaProxy::OnyxCompositedFrame), which copies what changed into the
window. A scroll paints only the rows that come into the window around the view.

Off by default: WKPreferencesSetCompositingEnabledOnyx before the view is made. The software
path is unchanged when it is off. Not yet: layers for CSS animations (only the root is composited;
an animation repaints its tile), groups, masks, rounded clips, 3D.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
